From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:25:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] ubox: logd: align each log entry to the header that
 follows it

logd pads its log entries to four bytes, but the header that starts the
next entry holds a struct timespec and needs eight-byte alignment on
64-bit targets: reading a misaligned header is undefined behaviour, and
logd traps within seconds of booting in a UBSan build on aarch64.

Add a patch to ubox that pads each entry to the header's alignment. It
is meant for ubox upstream.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 package/system/ubox/Makefile                  |  2 +-
 ...-entry-to-the-header-that-follows-it.patch | 29 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 package/system/ubox/patches/100-logd-align-each-log-entry-to-the-header-that-follows-it.patch

diff --git a/package/system/ubox/Makefile b/package/system/ubox/Makefile
index cccbf33..541b814 100644
--- a/package/system/ubox/Makefile
+++ b/package/system/ubox/Makefile
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=ubox
-PKG_RELEASE:=2
+PKG_RELEASE:=3
 
 PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
 PKG_SOURCE_URL=$(PROJECT_GIT)/project/ubox.git
diff --git a/package/system/ubox/patches/100-logd-align-each-log-entry-to-the-header-that-follows-it.patch b/package/system/ubox/patches/100-logd-align-each-log-entry-to-the-header-that-follows-it.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..df7fd14
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/system/ubox/patches/100-logd-align-each-log-entry-to-the-header-that-follows-it.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] logd: align each log entry to the header that follows it
+
+The log entries follow each other in the buffer, each a struct log_head
+and its message, padded to four bytes. The header holds a struct
+timespec, so it needs eight-byte alignment on 64-bit targets, and after
+a message whose padded length is four more than a multiple of eight the
+next header is misaligned: reading it is undefined behaviour. Built with
+-fsanitize=undefined -fsanitize-trap=undefined on aarch64, logd traps
+in log_next() within seconds of booting.
+
+Pad each entry to the alignment of struct log_head.
+
+Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/log/syslog.c
++++ b/log/syslog.c
+@@ -41,7 +41,10 @@
+ 
+ #define KLOG_DEFAULT_PROC	"/proc/kmsg"
+ 
+-#define PAD(x) (x % 4) ? (((x) - (x % 4)) + 4) : (x)
++/* Entries follow each other in the buffer: pad each to the alignment of the
++ * header that the next one starts with. */
++#define PAD(x) (((x) + __alignof__(struct log_head) - 1) & \
++		~(__alignof__(struct log_head) - 1))
+ 
+ static char *log_dev = LOG_DEFAULT_SOCKET;
+ static int log_size = LOG_DEFAULT_SIZE;
